{
  "slug": "project-pilot",
  "name": "Project Pilot",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Project Pilot is a Claude Code plugin that gives Claude a persistent memory layer for your project. It captures your architecture decisions, coding conventions, and current progress into a .pilot/ folder. Every new session starts with full context — no re-explaining, no re-discovering.\n\nIt works silently in the background. You code normally. Project Pilot tracks what changes, updates its knowledge, and warns you before you accidentally break something important.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 commands** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Commands** (3): `init-pilot` (Set up Project Pilot intelligence layer for this project — captures intent, conventions, architecture, and decisions into a…), `pilot-dashboard` (Return to a project after a break — re-orients you by reading the full .pilot/ context layer and…), `pilot-status` (Quick status report — shows current work, verified vs unverified features, known issues, pending decisions, and synthesis health…)\n- **Hooks** (4): `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `SessionStart`, `PreCompact`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install project-pilot@claude-community` from `David-Mazig/Project-Pilot`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "hook": 4,
    "command": 3
  },
